<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Paige, 73, comes for his subsequent annual wellness visit two weeks after a moderate COPD exacerbation; his last wellness visit was a year ago at his previous clinic. He finished the prednisone and doxycycline ten days ago and is back to his usual breathing, uses albuterol about once a day, and returned to pulmonary rehabilitation last week. He takes his umeclidinium-vilanterol every morning and atorvastatin every evening without muscle aches. He completed the health risk assessment beforehand. He wants all his vaccines today so that, in his words, the next cold does not knock him down. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit, age 73</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>COPD, GOLD 2, group B, recovered from a moderate exacerbation; hyperlipidemia on atorvastatin; former smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Umeclidinium-vilanterol daily; albuterol as needed; atorvastatin 20 mg</td></tr><tr><td>Mood and cognition</td><td>PHQ-2 0; Mini-Cog 5</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper in the waiting room and reviewed with him by Dr. Whitaker-Osei. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair to good; better since rehabilitation</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives with his wife; a large family nearby; active in his church; speaks at schools</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>A beer on a holiday; AUDIT-C 1 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Former smoker, about 30 pack-years, stopped eleven years ago; no secondhand smoke at home</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Pulmonary rehabilitation twice a week and walks on other days</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; weight steady</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours on two pillows by habit; no snoring reported</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at home</td><td>Smoke and carbon monoxide alarms; no firearms at home; gas stove used with the window open</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>No falls</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Reading glasses; hearing good</td></tr><tr><td>Oral health</td><td>Dentures; dental visit this year</td></tr><tr><td>Cost and access</td><td>The maintenance inhaler is covered through his drug plan with a low copayment; rides to rehabilitation from a church volunteer</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
