  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Breathlessness on exertion for about two years, now after one flight of stairs or a block on the level (mMRC 2), with a morning cough and a little clear sputum most days; no chest pain, ankle swelling, orthopnea, wheeze at rest or weight loss; a former smoker of about 30 pack-years; cause under evaluation with spirometry and a pulmonology consultation</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R06.09</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to his documented emphysema; superseded when spirometry at the consultation confirmed COPD.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, GOLD grade 2 (post-bronchodilator FEV1/FVC 0.58, FEV1 61% predicted by the race-neutral GLI Global equations), GOLD group B (CAT 18, mMRC 2, no exacerbation in the past year); alpha-1 antitrypsin normal; blood eosinophils 0.08 x 10^3/uL; synthetic modern diagnosis linked to his documented emphysema</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
