    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Fully recovered from the exacerbation. As a man of 65 to 75 who has smoked, he is due for one-time ultrasound screening for an abdominal aortic aneurysm. [S]<list><item>High-dose influenza, RSV and COVID-19 vaccines and the first recombinant zoster dose today; second zoster dose in two to six months.</item><item>Abdominal aortic ultrasound ordered.</item><item>Hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening drawn today.</item><item>Next wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">COPD exacerbation (J44.1)</content>. Resolved; back to his usual breathing. [S]<list><item>Group and treatment review at the fifteen-week visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>128/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid management</td><td>Up to date</td><td>LDL 86 mg/dL on atorvastatin 20 mg four weeks ago</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>HbA1c 5.6% at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Colonoscopy five years ago without polyps, reported by his previous clinic; further screening after 75 by shared decision</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Low-dose CT nine weeks ago, Lung-RADS 2; next in one year</td></tr><tr><td>Abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time ultrasound for men 65 to 75 who have ever smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>PSA screening is not recommended at 70 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Once for adults; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Triple panel once for all adults; drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Osteoporosis screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Evidence insufficient for screening men; one five-day steroid course does not change this; revisit if steroid courses recur</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 0</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5, normal</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Up to date</td><td>AUDIT-C 1 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Former smoker; remains smoke-free</td></tr><tr><td>Falls risk</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; Timed Up and Go 9 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine today</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Single dose today, for an adult 50 to 74 with chronic lung disease</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>This season&apos;s vaccine today after discussion</td></tr><tr><td>Zoster vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First recombinant dose today; second in two to six months</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 at intake; no further dose needed</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap at intake</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, high-dose, this season; Respiratory syncytial virus vaccine, single dose; COVID-19 mRNA vaccine, this season&apos;s formula; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for the Prevention, Diagnosis and Management of COPD: 2025 Report (2025); Lung Cancer: Screening (2021); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm: Screening (2019); Screening and Testing for Hepatitis B Virus Infection: CDC Recommendations — United States, 2023 (2023)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Fifteen-week review in three weeks. Aortic ultrasound and hepatitis results by then. Second zoster dose in two to six months. Next wellness visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-27: fifteen-week review after an exacerbation and pulmonary rehabilitation: symptoms, exacerbation history, GOLD group, oxygen, the action plan and the plan ahead. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
