    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 25 minutes, with his consent. He named a health care agent and a health care proxy form was completed; the agent is recorded in the chart and is not named here. He said that what matters most to him is staying at home in Kansas City, being with the people he loves, and still being able to talk with young players. If his lungs failed in a flare that could recover, he would accept a short trial of a breathing machine in intensive care, but not long-term life support if there were little chance of returning home. He will review these wishes with his family, and the plan will be revisited yearly or after any hospital stay. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
